# CODEOWNERS — review routing (T01-13).
#
# CODEOWNERS assigns required reviewers per path. The last matching pattern wins,
# so more specific rules are listed AFTER more general ones.
#
# The team handles below are PLACEHOLDERS. Real GitHub team handles are created
# and wired up under T01-14 (Auth, RBAC & Tenant Isolation) once teams exist.
# Until then these names document review *intent*; reviewers enforce it manually
# (see docs/operations/branching-and-release.md §7, §8).
#
#   @iPermit/engineering           — engineering owners (services, apps, infra, CI)
#   @iPermit/regulatory-analysts   — regulatory analyst group (rules and specs)

# Default: anything not matched below needs an engineering review.
*                                   @iPermit/engineering

# Engine and service code — engineering owners.
/services/                          @iPermit/engineering
/apps/                              @iPermit/engineering
/packages/                          @iPermit/engineering
/infrastructure/                    @iPermit/engineering
/scripts/                           @iPermit/engineering
/tests/                             @iPermit/engineering
/.github/                           @iPermit/engineering

# Regulatory rules — analyst group owns ALL rule data. Rule changes need an
# analyst reviewer who is not the drafting analyst (T00-09 §7).
/rules/                             @iPermit/regulatory-analysts

# Published and effective rules are writable only through the publication
# workflow (T08-04) and must not be edited by hand. Routing them to the analyst
# group makes any direct change require explicit analyst sign-off
# (AGENTS.md *Repository Strategy*; branching-and-release.md §8.3).
/rules/published/                   @iPermit/regulatory-analysts
/rules/effective/                   @iPermit/regulatory-analysts

# Regulatory specifications — analyst group owns the rule-object, jurisdiction,
# temporal, and SOP specs that govern how rules are authored.
/docs/specs/                        @iPermit/regulatory-analysts

# Strategic guardrails and roadmap — co-owned. Both groups must agree on changes
# to the locked decisions and the roadmap.
/AGENTS.md                          @iPermit/engineering @iPermit/regulatory-analysts
/docs/roadmap.json                  @iPermit/engineering @iPermit/regulatory-analysts
/docs/roadmap.md                    @iPermit/engineering @iPermit/regulatory-analysts
